<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Appuashu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Appuashu was king of Pirindu, a kingdom in the rugged west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, in the 6th century BCE. A Babylonian chronicle relates that in 557 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neriglissar">Neriglissar</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> defeated him, pursued him through the mountains and captured his cities, including Ura and his ancestral town of Kirshu. He is one of the few Cilician rulers of the period known by name.</p></div>
